SUMMARY:Our Lady's Saturday (sp)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: Red\n\nSt. Valentine\, Priest\, M\n\nLives of t
 he Saints — ST. VALENTINE, Priest and Martyr: VALENTINE was a lioly prie
 st in Pome, who, with St. Marius and his family, assisted the martyrs in t
 he persecution under Claudius II. He was apprehended, and sent by the empe
 ror to the prefect of Pome, who, on finding all his promises to make him r
 enounce his faith ineffectual, commanded him to be beaten with clubs, and 
 afterward to be beheaded, which was executed on the 14th of February, abou
 t the year 270. Pope Julius I. is said to have built a church near Ponte M
 ole to his memory, which for a long time gave name to the gate now called 
 Porta del Popolo, formerly Porta Valentini. The greater part of his relics
  are now in the Church of St. Praxedes. To abolish the heathens' lewd supe
 rstitious custom of boys drawing the names of girls, in honor of their god
 dess Februata Juno, on the 15th of this month, several zealous pastors sub
 stituted the names of Saints in billets given on this day.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
