SUMMARY:Ss. John & Paul\, Mm (d)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: Red\n\nWithin the Octave\nComplete Abstinence\n
 \nLives of the Saints — STS. JOHN AND PAUL, Martyrs: J^xHESB two Saints 
 were both officers in the army under \mJ Julian the Apostate, and received
  the crown of martyrdom, probably in 362. They glorified God by a double v
 ictory; they despised the honors of the world, and triumphed over its thre
 ats and torments. They saw many wicked men prosper in their impiety, but w
 ere not dazzled by their example. They considered that worldly prosperity 
 which attends impunity in sin is the most dreadful of all judgments ; and 
 how false and short-lived was this glittering prosperity of Julian, who in
  a moment fell into the pit which he himself had dug! But the martyrs, by 
 the momentary labor of their conflict, purchased an immense weight of neve
 r-fading glory ; their torments were, by their heroic patience and invinci
 ble virtue and fidelity, a spectacle worthy of God, Who looked down upon t
 hem from the throne of His glory, and held His arm stretched out to streng
 then them, and to put on their heads immortal crowns in the happy moment o
 f their victory.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
