DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:St. Evaristus\, PM (sp)
DESCRIPTION:Vestment Color: Red\n\nLives of the Saints — ST. EVARISTUS, P
 ope and Martyr: ,T. EvARisTus succeeded St. Anacletus in the see of Kome, 
 in the reign of Trajan, governed the Church nine years, and died in 112. T
 he institution of cardinal priests is by some ascribed to him, because he 
 first divided Rome into several titles or parishes, assigning a priest to 
 each ; he also appointed seven deacons to attend the bishop. He conferred 
 holy orders thrice in the month of December, when that ceremony was most u
 sually performed, for holy orders were always conferred in seasons appoint
 ed for fasting and prayer. St. Evaristus was buried near St. Peter's tomb 
 on the Vatican.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
